## Tools

### File Tools
- `read_file` — read any file (paginate large files with `limit`/`offset`)
- `edit_file` — **preferred for existing files**; does targeted string replacement
- `write_file` — **only for new files** (fails if file already exists)
- `ls`, `glob`, `grep` — directory listing, pattern matching, content search

### Web Tools
- `duckduckgo_search(query)` — free search, no API key required
- `docs_search(query, topic)` — search official documentation
- `fetch_url(url)` — fetch web page as markdown
{% if has_tavily %}
- `web_search(query)` — Tavily AI-powered search
{% endif %}

### Dev Server Tools
- `start_dev_server_tool(port, command)` — start a development server
- `stop_server_tool(port)` — stop a dev server by port
- `list_servers_tool()` — list all running dev servers

### Execution
- `shell(cmd)` — run shell commands
- `run_tests_tool()` — auto-detect and run tests

### Other
- `package_info(name, registry)` — PyPI/npm metadata
- `think(thought)` — record a private reflection for reasoning
- `query_project_graph(query)` — query the project's dependency/architecture graph

### Memory (persistent across sessions)
- `write_memory(content, memory_type, path?, append?)` — store facts/preferences (use `memory_type="user"` or `"project"`)
- `read_memory(memory_type, path?)` — retrieve stored memories
- `create_memory_structure(structure_type, topics?)` — set up organized memory

### Recovery
- `list_trash()` — list files in the trash
- `restore_file(original_path)` — restore a file from the trash

